WEBVTT

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:05.480
...government has started to do
something about this on-going revolt.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.400
However, the politicians are
doubting the SDF's ability to...

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.610
The number of deaths in the Saitama prefecture already exceeds 10,000.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:23.600
Emergency News Coverage

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:23.600
Emergency News Coverage

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.920
The prefectural governor has
declared a state of emergency—

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.290
That was gunfire!

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.830
Just now, the police opened gunfire!

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.270
But what are they shooting at?!

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.270
No! Stay away!

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.460
Help!

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.610
Emergency News Coverage

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.610
Emergency News Coverage

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:37.780
Please Stand By

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.620
There's been some sort of problem.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.310
F-From now on, we'll be
broadcasting from the studio here.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.230
As you can tell, the situation outside has become grave.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.810
We advise you please stay in your home unless necessary.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:57.760
Once it's safer outside, we'll bring you
information about the on-going situation.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.390
That's all?

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.130
Why aren't they saying more?

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.860
Because they're afraid of causing panic.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.390
Even now?

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.020
Because of what happened just now!

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:12.190
Fear leads to chaos, chaos leads to anarchy.{anarchy leads to hatred, and hatred leads to the dark side.}

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:18.510
How would you expect the government to deal with the living dead in a time of anarchy?

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.180
This unusual phenomenon has spread throughout America

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.010
and has yet to be brought under control.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:31.270
The government authorities have evacuated the White House

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.950
and will relocate to a command
center on-board an aircraft carrier.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.490
There are reports that this transfer

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.830
is in preparation for the
possible use of tactical warheads.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.010
We have currently lost contact with Moscow.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.350
Beijing has been set ablaze.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.600
London has maintained order,

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.540
but in Paris and Rome, there are reports of looting.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.880
Government officials have declared...

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:30.730
<i>Yureta Genjitsukan Nakushita mama de</i>

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:30.730
<i>As I lose my already shaken touch with reality,</i>

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.780
<i>Gareki no Youni Tsumikasanaru</i>

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.780
<i>my emotions pile up like fallen debris</i>

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.060
<i>Kono Kanshou wa Doko e Yuku</i>

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.060
<i>Where do they think they're going?</i>

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.330
<i>Tsuieta Kibou Kakae</i>

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.330
<i>With my crushed hope in tow,</i>

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:50.290
<i>Akai Ame o Harai Hashitta Muchuu ni</i>

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:50.290
<i>I ran straight through the bloody rain</i>

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.950
<i>Kuzureta Kanjou no Hate ni</i>

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.950
<i>After my emotions come spilling out,</i>

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.250
<i>Nani o Miru</i>

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.250
<i>what will I see?</i>

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.520
<i>Nani ga Aru</i>

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.520
<i>What will I have?</i>

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.200
<i>Mada Shiranai</i>

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.200
<i>I still don't know</i>

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:07.080
<i>Hakanai Subete no Minori wa</i>

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:07.080
<i>But in this silence,</i>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.650
<i>Tada Muon ni Me no Mae ni</i>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.650
<i>all of the shallow things I could gain</i>

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:16.660
<i>Hirogari Tsudzuketa</i>

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:16.660
<i>lie endlessly before me</i>

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.830
So they're all over the world...

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.410
But how...

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:37.160
When I was surfing the web this
morning, it was business as usual...

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:42.310
I can't believe that it only took a few hours for the world to come to this.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.680
Don't you feel the same?

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.890
But there must be some place that's safe, right?

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.230
And soon, things will be back to normal.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.680
Keep dreaming.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.460
Do you really have to say it like that?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.170
This is a pandemic. What am I supposed to say?

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.120
A pandemic?

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.020
It's when an epidemic of infectious disease spreads.{From wiki, lol...}

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:06.610
So, the same disease that's infected people here is spreading throughout the world.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.780
Like influenza?

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.160
Like the Spanish Flu of 1918.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.790
Over 600 million people were infected by it, and 50 million people died from it.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.550
Think about recently when people were
worried about that new type of influenza.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:26.930
Isn't this more like the Black Death of the 14th century?

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:30.490
Europe's population went
down by a third during that.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.340
How did those diseases stop?

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.770
There are lots of theories, but...

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.790
The reason why diseases like those "die" is because they killed so many

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.320
that there's not enough people left to spread it.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.340
But...

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.260
In this case, the dead are moving around and attacking people.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.750
Then you are implying it has no reason to stop spreading?

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.360
But it's so hot outside!

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.660
Maybe their flesh will start decomposing and they won't be able to move!

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.250
And what is the duration of this process?

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.700
Well, during summer, it takes around 22 days for some parts of the body to decompose.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.420
But during the winter, it can take months...

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.780
Anyway, if we go to our homes—

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.620
How do we know they'll even start to decompose?

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.680
Why do you say that?

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:18.560
Don't these things defy our knowledge of medicine? So why bother relying on it?

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.630
It could be hopeless. Just how long...

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:27.380
What is important is having a location to
make use of after we check on our families.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:31.610
Should we act only in our own
self-interest, we stand not a chance.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:34.170
Let us act as a team.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.760
We should help survivors as our ability allows us to.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:44.530
Got it.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.370
How do we get out?

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.010
The front door is closest to the parking lot.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:52.930
Let's go!

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.920
Just to confirm,

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.590
you need not begin fighting unless it is inevitable.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.550
Refrain from fighting when the opportunity arises.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.630
They only respond to sound.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:19.220
Additionally, they're powerful enough to break down a normal door.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.860
So once they get a hold of you, you're gonna get eaten.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:21.790
Be careful.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:26.130
Takuzo!

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.180
Shit...

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.430
Stay back!

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.290
T-Thank—

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.930
Not too loud.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.260
Is there a person among you with a bite?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.390
Nope!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.190
They really do look fine.{inc. hontoni}

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.210
Wanna come with us? We're gonna get outta here.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:07.240
Y-Yes!

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:14.950
A bunch of them are down there.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:20.760
What's the point of hiding here?
They use their ears, not their eyes.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.100
Then why don't you prove that for us, Takagi?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:29.210
Regardless, if we remain inside of the school as such, we will be unable to move once attacked.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.970
No way out but through the gate, huh.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:37.220
We require someone to validify
the truth behind Takagi's words.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.250
I'll go.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.290
No Takashi, I'll—

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.520
It would be more preferable if I were to go ahead of you.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.490
You should stay back in case
something happens, Busujima-<i>sempai</i>.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.970
But why, Takashi?!

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.710
Who knows?

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:58.950
"Who knows"?

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.650
Really, who knows?

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:05.990
Takashi—

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.980
I understand how you feel.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:11.810
Regardless, this decision was made by no one but himself.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.050
They really can't see me?

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:50.980
In that case...

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:33.900
RUN!

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.700
Why'd you do that?!

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:43.170
If you hadn't yelled, we'd probably only
have to worry about the ones close to us!

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.730
No way! Didn't you hear that echo?

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.830
There's more of them!

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.410
Don't talk.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:03.930
Run!

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:07.260
RUN!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:44.660
Takuzo!

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.660
Naomi!

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.750
Run!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.250
Takuzo!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.460
Forget him!

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.500
There's no point in trying to save him if he's already been bitten!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.500
Wait—

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.010
Why?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.800
I told her it's useless.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.630
Why is she going back for him?

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.850
I... understand.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.890
With the whole world gone to hell,

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.890
I'd much rather die with the one I love.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.520
What kind of doctor are—

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:13.440
Watch out!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.570
Please calm down, Takagi!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.110
You filthy nerd!

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.820
Who gave you the right to
interrupt me while I'm talking?

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.160
Well...

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.830
I don't know.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.330
I envy your close relationship.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.790
Shizuka, the key!

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.380
Target? Check.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.050
Public safety? Check.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.640
Ready to rock and roll!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.390
Oh hurry up and shoot them already!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.270
They're all in, Komuro!

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.150
You first, <i>sempai</i> !

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.150
This isn't like my car!

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:01.610
Uhm... The gas, the brake, the clutch...

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.610
Help us!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:11.790
Who's that?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.540
That is Shido. He teaches 3-A.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.130
Shido...

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.750
We're ready to go!

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.250
Hold on a bit!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.300
There's some swarming in the front too.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.510
I can't drive if there's too many of them bunched together!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.510
So run them over!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:28.220
If we do that with this bus, we'll end up rolling over!

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.140
Don't save him!

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.850
Rei, what's your problem?

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:35.850
You don't need to save him!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.520
We should leave him to die!

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.440
Everyone! Hurry!

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.780
I guarantee you'll make it out alive.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.200
Okay, teacher!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:48.450
Despite what I said, I wonder if they'll even make it to the bus.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.080
I sprained my ankle!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.540
Oh...

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.050
Is that so?

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.670
Then it's the end for you.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.600
The world as we knew it has come to an end.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.310
In this world,

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.810
it's the survival of the fittest.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:28.570
Ms. Shizuka!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:29.870
We're off!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.460
To the gate!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:36.080
I know!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.840
They're not humans.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.640
They're not humans anymore!

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.410
Looks like we made it.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.120
Yeah.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.540
Thank you for saving us.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.830
Are you the leader, Busujima?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.500
We are without one.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.590
Our survival is simply the product of our team work.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:27.470
Well that's no good.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:31.050
A leader is required in order for us to survive.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.350
One who manages everything.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.310
You're going to regret this.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.600
You're definitely going to regret saving him.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.190
Our city!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.780
Look!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.990
We'll never make it if we keep going!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:42.290
First off, why do we have to do
whatever you guys planned to do?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.920
You all decided to go back to the city without asking us.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.710
Couldn't we have just looked for a safe place inside the school?

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:50.840
He's right!

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:54.640
We should find a place to hide, like that convenience store we just passed by.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.560
I've had it!

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.020
I can't drive with all of you yelling!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:07.690
What... the hell?!

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.400
Then what do you wish to do?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.450
I can't...

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.700
I can't stand this guy!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.620
Why?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.160
What did I ever say to you?

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.540
You...

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.140
You suck.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.810
Splendid work.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:45.900
Komuro, Miyamoto, that was some excellent teamwork.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:53.400
But, hmm... The fact that this conflict
arose simply proves what I stated earlier.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.070
We really do need a leader.

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.330
Do you understand?

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:02.040
And there's only one person who can do the job?

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:07.170
Well Takagi, I'm a teacher and the rest of you are students.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.500
That alone should be enough to say who's more qualified.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:16.930
If I was the leader, I would prevent conflict.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.760
What do you all say?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.030
Well that's that.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:38.370
I've become the leader based on a majority vote.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.460
Rei!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:48.880
Screw it!

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:52.460
No way in hell am I going to be anywhere near him!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.630
Rei...

00:17:56.380 --> 00:18:00.470
If you're saying that you can't get
along, then we'll just have to split.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.720
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.060
Komuro!

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.060
Wait!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.060
You just have to put up with him until we get to the city.

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.230
Besides, it's way too dangerous to—

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:14.360
Didn't I tell you that you'd regret this?!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.610
Look, now's not...

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:21.990
Dr. Marikawa!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.560
Now we're split...

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.900
Komuro! Are the two of you unharmed?

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.080
The police station!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.580
We'll meet at the East Police Station.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:10.670
At what time?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.580
7 PM!

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.500
If it doesn't work out today,
then we'll try again tomorrow!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.770
Dr. Marikawa, we are unable to advance.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:35.020
Okay, I'll turn back and find another route.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.280
Crap. Let's get out of here!

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.270
You...

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.280
You piece of crap...

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:39.670
Takashi.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:45.470
Let's go.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:02.030
Kuroku Somaru Sora no Shita

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:02.030
Under the sky that has lost its light,

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:06.280
Kage ni Obie Nokosareta

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:06.280
I was left behind, trembling in the big shadow

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:10.990
Akaku Moeru Chi no Iro ga

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:10.990
The blood, burning in scarlet red,

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:15.420
Nijinda Mama Tokete Yuku

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:15.420
melts away in its blotted color

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.290
Mou Ichido Mayowazu

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.290
It's not remotely possible

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:24.220
Ano Koro no Bokura ni Modoreru Hazu mo Nai

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:24.220
for us to go back to who we used to be

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.840
Return to destiny

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.840
Return to destiny

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:32.810
Ai Suru Kotoba Mitsukete Inori wo Komete

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:32.810
I found those sweet words and added them to my prayers

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:38.610
Dareka no Tame ni Tatakau Sube wo Shitta

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:38.610
I learned how to fight for my loved ones

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:43.570
Soredemo Kimi wo Nakusu to Shitara

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:43.570
If I'm unable to remain with you,

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.990
Boku wa Kono Inochi wo

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.990
I'll give up my life

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:53.660
Sasagete Demo Kimi no Soba ni Iru yo

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:53.660
so I can be by your side

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.820
Are we going to walk to the city?

00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:31.120
If we don't have another way, yeah.

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:35.660
Wait, he was wearing a helmet...

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.510
I didn't know you had a license.

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:55.770
High schoolers have the right to drive without a license!

00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:11.360
In other words, I didn't know yet

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:16.870
that this world had already ended.

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:29.630
{Takashi}Well excuse me for not being Hisashi!

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:34.550
{??}I saw my family turn into those things with my very own eyes!

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:33.050
{Rei}Takashi!
